            <ArticleTitle>What has the baboon to offer as a model of experimental ischemia?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The greatest advantage of the baboon model is the phylogenetic closeness of the animal to man which may be of considerable importance when dealing with receptor-related events and with drug-specific therapy. The major disadvantage is the difficulty of dealing with awake baboons and the absence of any adequate model for coronary artery spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
